    2. Choose N in [4,6]. For each rect, pick (h,w) with max(h,w) in [1,10] and min(h,w) in [1,3], ensuring h+w <= 10. Reject if sum(max(h_i,w_i)) + N-1 > 30.
    3. Build input grid with height = max(max(h_i,w_i)), width = sum(w_i) + N-1. Place each rect top-aligned at its column offset, with 1-col bg gaps.
    4. Build output as 10 x (sum(max(h_i,w_i))+N-1) bg grid. Paint upper band (short x long, top-aligned) and lower band (long x short, bottom-aligned) with independent column cursors and 1-col gaps. Reject any dimension set where the resulting output footprints overlap.
